// Durable product actors — entities a user names, that survive restart, and that a Conversation,
// Mission or Council can be attributed to. At most ONE catalog may own them.
//
// Measured 2026-09-22 across ~400 Agent-named modules: Orca has none. Every "Agent" in the estate
// is one of three other things, and none of them is a durable product actor:
//
//   AgentStatusEntry      runtime, keyed by paneKey = `${tabId}:${leafId}`
//   ProviderType          provider classification (which vendor CLI)
//   AGENT_CATALOG         a hardcoded compile-time list of vendor CLIs, not a user roster
//   AgentTeam / TeamPane  transport (tmux pane layout)
//   AI Vault              a scanner over provider transcripts — "Agent Session History"
//
// So the list below is empty on purpose. W-C1 adds exactly one entry.
// Enforced by `pnpm check:durable-actor-catalogs`.
{
  "actorCatalogs": []
}
